From fcd67d503d03c6d318379dacf012a584e58a65d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ada Lundhe <adalundhe@lundhe.audio>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:58:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sys: FileLinkInformation: forward hard links to a file
 system that declares VolumeParams.HardLinks

A volume that sets HardLinks now receives FileLinkInformation and FileLinkInformationEx as a SetInformation request
in the rename request's layout: Info.Rename.NewFileName is the new name, Info.RenameEx.Flags carries ReplaceIfExists
(bit 0) and, for FileLinkInformationEx where SupportsPosixUnlinkRename is set, FILE_LINK_POSIX_SEMANTICS and
FILE_LINK_IGNORE_READONLY_ATTRIBUTE, and Info.Rename.AccessToken is the requestor's token when a name may be replaced.
A directory answers STATUS_FILE_IS_A_DIRECTORY, a deleted file STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, a stream STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
a name that may be replaced must have no open handle (FspFileNodeRenameCheck, as a rename's target).

On success the file's cached information is invalidated (its link count changed), a replaced name's file node leaves
the name table as FspFileNodeRename makes one leave, the new name's directory listing is invalidated and its watchers
are told FILE_ACTION_ADDED. The completion runs on the file system's answering thread, so it acquires no other file
node.

NumberOfLinks (FileStandardInformation, FileAllInformation, FileStatInformation, FileStatLxInformation) is the file
system's FSP_FSCTL_FILE_INFO.HardLinks where the volume declares HardLinks and the count is nonzero; otherwise 1, and
always 1 for a directory, as on NTFS. A volume that does not declare HardLinks answers as before:
FileLinkInformation STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED, FileLinkInformationEx STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER.
